<title>FINLAND: POSTIPANKKI SETS TWO FIM 200 MLN BONDS.</title>
<headline>POSTIPANKKI SETS TWO FIM 200 MLN BONDS.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish state-owned commercial bank Postipankki Oy said on Thursday it would issue two 200 million markka bonds targetted at the public.</p>
<p>One is a four-year bond with a 3.75 percent coupon, and the other is a six-year bond with 4.50 percent coupon, Postipankki said.</p>
<p>The issue price on both bonds is variable.  </p>
<p>The subscription period is March 17 to May 2, 1997, Postipankki said in a statement.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
